  "worked_solution": "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $3$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3F+\\frac{1}{2}G & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 1 & 3\\cdot 3 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-2) & 3\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3+1 & 9+0 \\\\ -6+2 & 6+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
